---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentPage from "../../components/ContentPage.astro";
import Feature from "../../components/Feature.astro";
import SideImage from "../../components/SideImage.astro";
import Sc from "../../components/Sc.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Xuanhai">
    <ContentPage
        title="玄海 Xuanhai"
        description="Venerable of the moon, god of rain, venerated across the continent"
        backHref="/"
    >
        <h2>The Rain God, Xuanhai</h2>
        
        <p>
            <i>Fortune born the brothers of the moon, gods of the rain. He who controls
                the water, brings bounty and harvest, and takes all under heaven as his
                children.</i>
        </p>

        <Feature
            image={import("../../content/albums/chars/yushen-ref.jpg")}
            alt="Xuanhai reference sheet"
            title="Reference sheet"
        />

        <p>
            The rain god "Xuanhai" is the elder of two brothers, born from one egg in ancient
            times atop the divine mountain of Damak Dai. He is half divine, his father the Dragon
            creator god Xiron.
        </p>
        <SideImage
            image={import("../../content/albums/chars/moon-god-temple.jpg")}
            caption="The Rain God's temple portrait"
            right
            maxWidth="400px"
        />
        <p>
            In that ancient era, the skies were chaotic and ever-changing, just as the rivers
            and mountains were orderly. That was as <Sc>Asyr</Sc>, who created the heavens, was
            the embodiment of chaos and disorder, and <Sc>Xiron</Sc>, who created the earth,
            was the embodiment of order and harmony.
        </p>
        <p>
            Xuanhai and his brother Canghai, seeing the suffering of the
            common people, and the wild and unenlightened nature of their own kind, wished to
            use their power to help all under heaven. Defying heaven, they commanded the
            primordial sky to calm, creating peace and prosperity. In the night they became twin
            moons that shone calming light, suppressing the ghosts and terrors that lurk in the 
            darkness.
        </p>
        <p>
            Hence the heavens were calmed, and people rejoiced, giving the brothers incense and prayer; 
            however this act that defied heaven, defied the creator <Sc>Asyr</Sc>, brought her ire
            down upon them. As they were of divine blood, "family" even in a sense, she could not
            just kill them, hence she exiled the younger brother far overseas, and imprisoned the elder
            brother atop Damak Dai, decreeing that neither would see each other again. From that point on,
            the weather became a compromise of primordial chaos and controlled order; the younger brother
            was slowly forgotten save for in legends, and only one moon shone in the night.
        </p>

        <p>
            "Xuanhai" and "Canghai" were style names picked by the brothers themselves. Their draconic
            names were long lost to time. Even the name "Xuanhai" today is uknown, as the tradition of 
            name taboo has lead to it being avoided to such an extent that he is only known by the title
            "Rain God" or "Moon Venerable".
        </p>

        <h3>漢文注釋</h3>

        <p>
            二神漢文本字曰：玄海、滄海。玄海長兄，滄海幼弟。今茲字大失。凡人避諱，不敢直呼。久而久之，但言
            尊號，或曰雨神或曰月尊。
        </p>

        <hr></hr>

    </ContentPage>
</BaseLayout>
